      "card_ids": ["C82", "C83", "C84", "C85", "C86", "C87", "C88", "C89", "C90", "C91", "C92", "C93"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists.",
    "No query-specific fed-state pharmacokinetic or food-effect data are available.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic-stability measurement exists; L6 records are for midazolam, bupropion, and diazepam/temazepam.",
    "P-gp substrate status of the query is unknown.",
    "High logP/logD and low predicted solubility remain physicochemical concerns but are not affirmative evidence for F <20%.",
    "Structural transferability is qualitative; no numeric similarity score is supplied."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high. Human absolute F values for structurally related N-methyl quinolinone/heteroaromatic chlorophenyl drugs (tasquinimod, doravirine, triazolobenzodiazepines, trazodone, fasudil) are all well above 20%; L3-L5 exposure/permeability records support high absorption for lipophilic heteroaromatic compounds; L6 hepatic-clearance records are for other molecules and do not affirmatively establish F<20% for the query. Fed state is not expected to negate the high prediction based on available analog food-effect data."
}

